# pr-lifecycle-workflow-edits.patch
#
# Restores the spec-driven-pr PR-lifecycle edits to OpenSpec's stock
# openspec-apply-change / openspec-archive-change skills (and their
# opsx: command twins) after `openspec update` overwrites them.
#
# These edits teach apply to discover and surface any post-tasks artifact
# (e.g. a `pr` artifact) generically - via `openspec status --json`'s
# `artifacts` list, never a hardcoded id - and teach archive to reconcile
# that artifact's external status (via delegation to whatever skill its
# `instruction` field names) as a hard safety check before archiving, not
# just an advisory suggestion.
#
# Apply with:
#   git apply openspec/patches/pr-lifecycle-workflow-edits.patch
#
# Verify afterward:
#   1. grep -n "pr\.md\|openspec-pr-lifecycle\|\`pr\` artifact" \
#        .claude/skills/openspec-archive-change/SKILL.md \
#        .claude/commands/opsx/archive.md
#      -> should show ZERO matches (archive must stay schema-agnostic,
#         discovering the artifact structurally rather than by name)
#   2. Create a throwaway change on spec-driven-pr, confirm the `pr`
#      artifact is discovered generically and apply step 7 surfaces its
#      instruction field once tasks are all done.
#   3. Create a throwaway change with a fake pr.md, confirm archive
#      step 2.5 discovers it generically and delegates reconciliation
#      to the openspec-pr-lifecycle skill rather than reading/writing
#      pr.md or calling GitHub itself.
#   4. Delete the throwaway change(s) afterward.
#
# See CONTRIBUTING.md's "Maintenance note: openspec update" section.

diff --git a/.claude/commands/opsx/apply.md b/.claude/commands/opsx/apply.md
index 66164d5..d6347fa 100644
--- a/.claude/commands/opsx/apply.md
+++ b/.claude/commands/opsx/apply.md
@@ -105,7 +105,7 @@ Implement tasks from an OpenSpec change.
    Display:
    - Tasks completed this session
    - Overall progress: "N/M tasks complete"
-   - If all done: if the schema defines a `pr` artifact (check `openspec status --change "<name>" --json`), suggest opening a PR via the `openspec-pr-lifecycle` skill; otherwise suggest archive
+   - If all done: run `openspec status --change "<name>" --json` and look at `artifacts` for any entries beyond the ones `apply` just finished (i.e. artifacts not in `applyRequires`, now showing `ready`) - do not assume a specific id like `pr`, just check what the schema itself reports as the next ready artifact(s). For each such artifact, run `openspec instructions <artifact-id> --change "<name>" --json` and surface its `instruction` field to the user verbatim as the next-step suggestion (this is the schema's own canonical guidance, which may delegate to a skill or may not - follow whatever it says rather than hardcoding a skill name). If there is no such artifact, suggest archive
    - If paused: explain why and wait for guidance

